  data: {
    LLM: "In positive contracts, aim for 36+ points. Protect high-value cards (kings, honours). Remember the SkÃ¼s, XXI, and I are each worth 5 points plus their trick value.\n\nTalon selection is crucial. Look for packets containing kings or high trumps. When calling a king, call one you don't have - if it appears in talon, you play alone (often disadvantageous).\n\nBird Strategy: Announcing Pagat Ultimo, Uhu, Kakadu, or Marabu doubles their value but commits you to a specific play. Only announce if you have strong position. In negative contracts (Bettel, Piccolo), card play becomes inverted - you're trying to lose tricks, which requires understanding opponents' hands.",
    Player: "In positive contracts, aim for 36+ points. Protect high-value cards (kings, honours). Remember the SkÃ¼s, XXI, and I are each worth 5 points plus their trick value.\n\nTalon selection is crucial. Look for packets containing kings or high trumps. When calling a king, call one you don't have - if it appears in talon, you play alone (often disadvantageous).\n\nBird Strategy: Announcing Pagat Ultimo, Uhu, Kakadu, or Marabu doubles their value but commits you to a specific play. Only announce if you have strong position. In negative contracts (Bettel, Piccolo), card play becomes inverted - you're trying to lose tricks, which requires understanding opponents' hands.",
